        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Eastern Market, Detroit, Michigan, The Old Red Barn\n- People: Pete Cusimano, Jerry Cusimano\n- Events: Legend of the Octopus\n- Concepts: historic commercial districts, U.S. regions\n\nFacts:\n- Eastern Market is a historic commercial district in Detroit, Michigan.\n- Michigan is a state in the Great Lakes and Midwestern regions of the United States.\n- On April 15, 1952, Pete Cusimano and Jerry Cusimano, brothers and storeowners in Detroit's Eastern Market, started the Legend of the Octopus practice by throwing an octopus onto the rink of The Old Red Barn.",
